      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I made a feedback post but I guess it's already noted here - elbows either flare out way behind shoulder or they aggressively spaz out. With tweaks you can turn off elbow chest avoidance to stop the spazzing but the elbow flare still presists. Happens with every avatar I try even the vrchat defaults, not one works properly when comparing to legacy ik. For me personally it makes the new ik worse for general use than legacy, but I tend to like to dance in VR, a lot of people probably havent clocked how bad it really is. Video showing the issue https://youtu.be/Vw8OMG2gnCg also the pics, first is legacy, second is new ik, third is the position my arm is in for all the tests.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
